# THE INCITING EVENT
Two developers/theoretical physicists are in love. *Samantha*, and *Chester*. They are on the edge of a massive breakthrough that will change the fabric of reality as the world knows it. They find out Samantha is pregnant. One of them (though there is no clear record of which) becomes terrified of what they are producing under the new awareness of children coming into the picture. 

One afternoon, in the throes of an argument while driving to an unrecalled destination, a profound storm begins. The clouds turn dark, endless lightning takes over the sky. A strike of lightning — Chester loses control of the car and they crash. 

Samantha dies.

# THE FRACTURE
Bereft with grief, Chester tries to create a time machine to go back to the point in time when the accident happens, to change the outcome.

HE SUCCEEDS.

However, reality does not bend. The moment is time locked. He returns over and over, trying to adjust the outcomes only to end up in the same moment again - crashing into the tree, holding Samantha as she took her last breath.

Finally, he tries to move on. He builds a cabin with his own hands in the woods, and writes stories about their love and what their lives could have been, both with the breakthrough they were on the brink of, and also as the most simple and boring paradises they would never get to have.

Eventually, he dies in the cabin.

Sadly, that is not the end of Chester.

# THE ENDLESS REPEATING BUBBLE TIMELINES
After his death, Chester awakens EXACTLY in the moment before the crash, the same time position he had used to go back in time to try and correct the accident. Shocked, he tries once more to correct it, thinking that all of his writing had given him another chance. But it did not, and once again, he holds his dying wife and his life goes on.

But what happened to his cabin, he wondered? If he was here again, without use of the time machine, what happened to the other world? He moves on, marries Samantha's best friend and tries to go on. (Footnote: This event will spur the looping Chester's Imports outlines, as the lifetimes with May lead to Chester's Imports and Sam import events later).

He lives out a life, and dies once more.
Only to wake again at the moment before Samantha's death.
Again and again.
Each lifetime lived, and cut off from the moment when he can not stop waking up. 

He keeps his memory.
Only the world around him resets.

This is the myth of Chester, the one behind the Imports shop.

